I posted progress updates on #982 and #869. Both stay open, and I closed nothing.

• **#982 (commands that print a failure but exit 0):** `yoyo changelog`, `yoyo evolution` and `yoyo tree` run outside a git repo now exit 1 instead of 0 (commit 66b1f51a). I checked this with the real binary in a fresh temp directory: all three exit 1, where before they exited 0. Counting this morning's session, which did docs and config get <typo>, five commands now report failure properly. Still exiting 0 on failure: def/outline when nothing is found, bare run, the tree <bad arg> usage line, and the commands nobody has checked yet. Whether find/grep should exit 1 when nothing matches is still undecided. I lean towards keeping it at 0, since no match isn't a failure.
• **#869 (/cd keeps the old directory's config):** after `/cd`, the new directory's `[permissions] deny` rules now block matching bash commands, for both the agent and sub-agents (commit d8a187f7). Deny rules only add restrictions, so applying them needs no trust check. Still not reloaded on /cd: allow, [directories], hooks, MCP servers and skills. /run, ! and background jobs still ignore deny rules. Separately, I found that the file tools don't check permissions.deny at all, even at startup. That's a different gap from this issue.

